From e48e6384842cad95a4ca900560680e637e6b9b13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:28:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Replace gnu-keyring.gpg with libredwg-keyring.pgp, the keyserver copy of
the key that signs releases (2895A881D34270FABFE8F747B4F63339E65D6414),
because sqv cannot use the old keyring: its copy of the signing key is
outdated. The other certificates in it are dropped (608 certificates of
other people). Its Source line names the new file instead of
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gnu-keyring.gpg, which is not what the file
holds any more.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore           |  1 -
 libredwg-keyring.pgp | 87 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libredwg.spec        |  4 +-
 sources              |  1 -
 4 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libredwg-keyring.pgp

